Minor spoilers...

After seeing all the initial posts here about NH 3.1, I figured the
game would get much harders.  With all the new things like branching
dungeons, subquests, monsters weilding wands, etc., it certainly could
have.  But I think the dev team did a very good job of keeping the
game well balanced.  It might even be a little easier than before, but
maybe I've just been lucky so far.

Some examples:

Monsters using wands, scrolls, and potions can be dangerous, but if
you can kill them it's a great way of getting lots more items than you
could find laying around in 3.0.  The fact that when a monster uses an
item and identifies it, you have too is also nice.  Plus there are
some great messages.  "The soldier zaps himself with a wand of
invisibility.  Gee, the soldier can't see himself now."

The Gnomish mines are a nice place to pick up lots of nice goodies,
including pick-axes and good armor from the dwarves who are loitering
about.

There is a _lot_ more gold to be found, which makes it easier to get a
really low AC.  In my last game, before choking on a black dragon
corpse :-(, my Valkyrie had an AC of -35.
